course: dictionary
lesson: 5767
title: Lunch: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lunch is a word you use every school day, but it can mean different things. It can be the meal you eat, the time you eat it, or the food you bring from home. The words around it show you which meaning is right.
explain: «When Lily's usual friends fall out and leave her alone, Sam sits with her at lunch.» Here lunch is a time, the middle of the school day. Sam is not eating a meal; he is sitting with Lily during that time. Try swapping in "at lunchtime" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Jayden forgot his homework, owned up to his teacher, did it at lunch and missed playtime.» Lunch is a time again. The clues are "did it at" and "missed playtime", which show that lunch comes before playtime.
fact: Lunch is a noun: it can be a meal, as in «school lunches», or a time, as in «at lunch».
fact: A packed lunch is food you take from home in a box or bag.
fact: To lunch is a formal verb meaning to eat lunch.
fact: A good lunch has fruit or vegetables, some protein and water.
fact: The school canteen, also called the cafeteria, is where many children have their school lunch.
exercise: «A teacher says his family owes $12 for school lunches.» In this sentence, what is a lunch? | A packed box | *A meal | A verb meaning to eat | A time of day
exercise: «Sam sits with her at lunch.» What is lunch here? | To eat | A meal from home | *A time of day | A school bag
exercise: What is a packed lunch? | A meal cooked by the school | A kind of playtime | *Food you take from home in a box or bag | A bell that rings at noon
test: In «They lunched together after the match», what kind of word is lunched? | A noun, a thing | *A verb, a doing word | An adjective, a describing word | A time marker
test: Which lunch follows the health tip in the dictionary? | Only sweets and fizzy drink | A bag of crisps and nothing else | Nothing at all, to save time | *An apple, a cheese sandwich and water
exam: Read «Jayden did it at lunch and missed playtime.» Is lunch a meal or a time here, and how do you know? | A packed box from home | *A time, because he did his homework during it and then missed playtime | A meal, because he ate something | A verb, because it follows at
